<<~ ahu #head >>

! Persona-Policy ~ one face out, the multitude within

The multi-persona identity core (persona-circle: a human as a private Circle of selves, each an all-hardened key at its own handle-index) ''carries three operator rulings'' that fix how a vessel wears its selves and how it recovers them. Each ruling ''bends toward the same law'': the mesh refuses a global identity-now, so it never builds the Single Identity Number even to defend itself. <<~ confidence Synthesis-Canon 15/20 >> The rulings land 2026-07-20, dispatched to code at #64 stage 4.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #one-face >>

!! Ruling 1 ~ one face to the mesh, reboot to switch (PRIVATE-all, PUBLIC-one)

''A vessel shows the mesh ONE face at a time.'' The public/carry seam serves ''only the WORN persona''; the human's own private pool sees ''all N''. So the disclosure asymmetry reads: ''PRIVATE-all, PUBLIC-one'' — the multitude stays whole inside, one persona reaches outward.

''Switching a persona REBOOTS into the new identity'' — never a live hot-swap. The active-persona pointer ''reads at BOOT'': `wearPersona` sets it, the boot reads it, and the vessel re-stands AS that persona. This matches the built selector exactly (the mask you put on holds until you take it off and re-stand the house beneath). //"No two equals the same"// (Principia Discordia): each boot re-enacts a ''distinct identity-instance'', never a fused continuity across the switch.

The wall stays custody-by-TYPE: wearing a persona ''REQUIRES that this vessel HOLD its sovereign root'' — you sign only as a self whose secret you carry (persona-vault#wearPersona).

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #cryptographic-individual >>

!! Ruling 2 ~ each PersonaGroup a cryptographic individual (Sybil-of-one, the accepted cost)

''You CANNOT pin "one human = one custodian" in crypto — that pinning IS the sin.'' A cryptographic layer that asserted "these N faces trace to one person" would rebuild the global identity-now the mesh forbids (the Nymwars root, persona-circle#the-vault). So the ruling ''declines the pin'': each ''PersonaGroup stands as its OWN cryptographic individual'', with its own root, its own device-delegation edge, and its own escrow (#distinct-recovery).

''A human faking a cabal of their own PersonaGroups — a Sybil-of-one — reads as the ACCEPTED COST'' of the inversion-of-control. The crypto ''prices'' Sybil per-scope; it never eliminates it (persona-circle#honest-scope: scarcity lives outside the math). The answer runs ''SOCIAL, never cryptographic'': ''kahu as custodians, NOT rulers'' — vouch-and-price, exit-not-voice, legitimacy-held-in-talk-story (cabal-place#the-unswept-corner; carry-contract#the-frame). The mesh ''holds the residual adversary in story tension'' rather than pretending a signature closes it. <<~ confidence Synthesis-Canon 14/20 >>

The honest wall stays lit, dual to the wax-stamp's: ''"a valid key" reads as crypto fact; "one person behind these keys" does NOT'' — and the mesh ''wants it that way'', because the alternative wears N masks over a smuggled root.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #distinct-recovery >>

!! Ruling 3 ~ distinct recovery custodians per persona

''Each persona recovers through its OWN custodians.'' Shared custodians across personas would ''correlate them'' — a custodian holding shares for both Guru-Josh and Telarus-KSC learns they name one human, and web2's global-now walks back in through the recovery door. So the recovery split runs ''PER persona-root'' (persona-vault: a persona-1 quorum reconstructs persona-1's root, never persona-0's), and the ''custodian sets stay disjoint'' by ruling. Recovery re-admits a device; it never re-fuses the selves.

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #two-layer-petnames >>

!! The Two-Layer Pet-Names ~ private label ⊥ public glamour (Zooko)

A persona carries ''two names beside its key'', and the key stays the only global one. ''Zooko's triangle resolves'' the same way handle-card proves it: the ''GLOBAL name STAYS the pubkey'' — the veiled-user key the persona-HD tree derives — secure-and-decentralised because it IS the key; ''memorability rides a LOCAL name'':

* ''The OWN side ~ the private pet-name map'' (`{handleIndex -> petname}`, persona-petname). The human's own label for their own faces — "work", "the-guru", "my-burner" — ''freely renamable'' and ''NEVER federated''. It names the inside of the private Vault to its keeper alone. The wall runs structural: no board write exists in the seam. A ''multitude-view'' reads the whole self across the vessel — `{persona → pet-name, held-here?, has-public-handle?}` — so the human sees every face while the mesh sees one.
* ''The OTHER side ~ the handle-book'' (handle-book). The recogniser's local labels for ''OTHERS'' nyms' — never on any wire.
* ''The ONLY name that federates ~ the public glamour'' (persona-glamour). The persona's veiled key ''signs a HandleCard'' whose `glamour` shows a chosen display (never a legal identity); it ''announces onto the per-Nexus @crossroads WHO board'' (who-face), self-certifying, monotone-versioned, leased against the local clock.

''Three stores, never fused'': private-own (pet-name) ⊥ public-own (glamour record) ⊥ others (handle-book). The pet-name map ''wants to sync'' across the human's own PersonaGroup vessel-pool — private-federated over a PRIVATE BAG — but that ride waits on the ''device-fleet'' (not yet built; blocks on Beelay). So the seam stands ''LOCAL-FIRST'', shaped so the cross-pool sync drops into the same store shape when the fleet lands. <<~ confidence Synthesis 12/20 >>

<<~/ahu >>

<<~ ahu #no-global-now-for-identity >>

!! The Deep Frame ~ no global-now for identity

The three rulings ''share one root'': the causal-islands law (#causal-islands: no global present, each island its own partial log) ''extended to IDENTITY''. There sits ''no global now for who-someone-is'' — no mesh-wide instant of "this human = these faces = one custodian". Every attempt to assert it manufactures the very global-now the substrate forbids (the same move carry-contract's immune system refuses for revocation, one plane over).

So the mesh ''declines to build the SIN even to defend itself''. It could bind personas to one custodian and catch the Sybil-of-one — and it ''MUST NOT'', because that catch IS the sin it refuses. The residual adversary (a human forging a cabal of their own selves) stays ''bounded where a mythos wants it'': answered by ''kahu as custodians not rulers'' (vouch, price, watch, exit), by ''fork-as-exit'' (cabal-place: leave the captured place, re-point your own petname), and by ''legitimacy-held-in-talk-story'' — never by a signature claiming a global identity-now. //Shadowland's refusal made law//: the net heals faster than the corps can burn a runner, and it never installs the corps' own registry to do it.

<<~/ahu >>

